+
+## 4. Lifecycle & Flows
+
+### Round lifecycle (`rounds.status`)
+
+- **`open`** ΓÇö judges enter/submit sheets (event must be `ready`, round `open`).
+  Tabulator sees the monitor grid (counts only).
+- **`closed`** ΓÇö tabulator action (audited). Unsubmitted sheets are blocked from
+  submitting. The review screen becomes available: computed standings (via the
+  pure core, inside `score.manage`-gated functions only), tie-resolution
+  controls, advancement cut preview + overrides.
+- **`published`** ΓÇö tabulator action (audited). Runs the full compute +
+  validation (ties must be resolved ΓåÆ else `TIES_UNRESOLVED`; advancement
+  config must be satisfiable), inserts `resultVersions` v1, patches round
+  status. Results now visible per ┬º2. Terminal for the round.
+- **`closed ΓåÆ open` reopen** ΓÇö allowed while unpublished (audited); re-enables
+  pending submissions.
+
+### Event lifecycle
+
+- **`ready ΓåÆ finalized`** ΓÇö `finalize event` mutation: requires every round
+  `published`; patches event status to `finalized`, which locks the ability to
+  create new result versions or move the event back. Audited. Event-final
+  cross-round standings are **computed on read** by a query over published
+  round versions (┬º5 step 7) ΓÇö all inputs are immutable, so the query is
+  deterministic and cheap; no separate event-final snapshot is stored.
+- **`finalized ΓåÆ archived`** and **`ready ΓåÆ archived`** ΓÇö as in Phase 2.
+- **`ready ΓåÆ draft` reopen (Phase 2) is tightened:** refused (`CONFLICT`) once
+  any sheet is `submitted`/`locked` or any round is beyond `open`. This
+  protects the immutable score history from the sheet-deleting reopen path.
+
+### Score entry flow (judge)
+
+1. Judge opens `scoring` ΓåÆ sees only rounds/categories/criteria in their
+   assignment scope where sheets exist for them.
+2. Opens a contestant sheet ΓåÆ criteria list with min/max/precision hints.
+3. Keystrokes debounced ΓåÆ `saveDraft` patches `sheet.draftValues` (valid values
+   only; sheet status ΓåÆ `in_progress`).
+4. **Submit** ΓÇö validates: every in-scope criterion present, each within
+   `[minScore, maxScore]` at `decimalPrecision`; inserts one `scores` row per
+   criterion, patches sheet status `submitted`, clears `draftValues`, writes
+   audit (`score.submitted`), stamps `submittedAt/By`. Strictly immutable
+   afterward ΓÇö no mutation exists that can alter or delete these rows.
+
+### Correction flow (tabulator, post-publish)
+
+- `resultVersions` correction mutation: requires round `published` + event not
+  `finalized`; inserts version N+1 ΓÇö a superseding standings snapshot produced
+  under the same deterministic core (e.g. after an advancement-decision
+  change) ΓÇö plus a required `reason`; audited. Scores rows are never touched:
+  corrections document judging outcomes, not score edits.
+
